 ## Background
-The concept of brick-based caching with LRU replacement originated in the context of real-time ray-casting of discrete isosurfaces, where decoupling volume size from GPU resolution restrictions was necessary [S1]. The specific implementation details, including the MMU structure and `cnt_buf` optimization, are documented in open-source projects and academic works on parallel volume rendering [S2, unofficial]. The integration with residency octrees and GPU-steered management further evolved the technique to handle multi-resolution hierarchies and web-based rendering scenarios [S4][S5, S6, unofficial].
+The concept of brick-based caching with LRU replacement originated in the context of real-time ray-casting of discrete isosurfaces, where decoupling volume size from GPU resolution restrictions was necessary [S1]. The specific implementation details, including the MMU structure and `cnt_buf` optimization, are documented in open-source projects and academic works on parallel volume rendering [S2, unofficial]. The integration with residency octrees and GPU-steered management further evolved the technique to handle multi-resolution hierarchies and web-based rendering scenarios [S3, unofficial].
 
